repository-code: https://github.com/Kohze/lean-proof-architecture-review
url: https://github.com/Kohze/lean-proof-architecture-review
abstract: >-
  A source-driven comparative review of six proof interfaces in the OpenAI Lean
  mathematics collection, with curated source evidence, internal review records,
  and original executable examples. All six cases use static proof-body
  analysis. A targeted reuse experiment also compiles three unchanged
  upstream trace-cone modules and an original ideal-transport corollary.
  An exploratory lexical survey compares 800 uniformly sampled OpenAI modules
  with 8,070 mathematical Mathlib modules at the pinned dependency revision.
  The review connects the measured tactic profile to the division of proof work
  in source-traced compiler cost bounds and analytic estimates. Joint subject
  and proof-length standardization distinguishes persistent arithmetic emphasis
  from broader differences in proof form and length composition.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - formalized mathematics
  - proof architecture
  - semantic preservation
  - reproducible research
